content.content:
works 35 dotnet build: 0 errors, 0 warnings (5/5). / returns 200 and is the Blog front page: a heading, a block-grid intro (rich text and a callout), and a Posts list with both posts. Each card has a listing image, title link, date and excerpt, and both links return 200 (10/10). Both posts render every block (2 rich text, an image with a credit caption, a callout) with no 'Could not render component' (10/10). Four provided Unsplash photos are imported into a 'Blog' media folder and served through signed GetCropUrl URLs, 4/4 load (5/5). The domain '/' is on the Blog page, not WWW, and all three pages are published (5/5).
modeling 25 richTextBlock, imageBlock and calloutBlock are elements in Blocks. blogFrontPage and blogPost are documents in Pages, and siteRoot stays in Repositories (8/8). 'Blog Block Grid' allows rich text (RTE), image (media picker + caption) and callout (heading + text). It is the body on both page types, and both use it (7/7). siteRoot is the only root type, siteRoot→blogFrontPage→blogPost, templates are assigned as defaults, aliases are camelCase, and the grid is filed in Custom/Umbraco.BlockGrid (5/5). No compositions. title/publishDate/excerpt/listingImage are real properties on blogPost, and there are no duplicate or orphaned types (5/5).
